{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "Well... I could always go for some exercise. Maybe we could go to the batting cages...": "",
  "Or maybe we could play some darts?": "",
  "(Those are some good options. Now which one should we go with?)": "",
  "Oh, that'd be great! I can't wait to check it out!": "",
  "Why don't we hit the batting cages? I could use a little exercise myself.": "",
  "Great! I haven't been in quite a while.": "",
  "I'm feeling more like darts today.": "",
  "Sounds good to me. Will we take turns or play against each other?": "",
  "Let's play each other. I hope you don't mind a challenge.": "",
  "Not at all. I just hope you give me one!": "",
  "Ahh... Now that was what I call a good time.": "",
  "Maybe we could sit down somewhere and chat for a bit?": "",
  "Yeah, that sounds good. We have been standing all day.": "",
  "That, and I promised I'd take you out. You currently have one free meal remaining.": "",
  "Haha, all right then. Where should we go?": "",
  "(I wonder how she feels about drinking on the first date... Maybe I should just go for it?)": "",
  "I'm thinking we should drink. What do you say?": "",
  "Wow, you totally read my mind! Let's do it!": "",
  "(Why is it that my mind always wanders to alcohol when it comes to having a good time...)": "",
  "Call me crazy, but I kinda feel like having a drink right now.": "",
  "A drink? Right now? Honestly, Nanami-san... I could go for that.": "",
  "Oh, so you're a drinker then?": "",
  "About as much as anyone else.": "",
  "(Hah! I'm a genius.)": "",
  "How about we try this place out?": "",
  "Sure! Let's do it!": "",
  "So, Nanami-san. Tell me a little about yourself.": "",
  "Okay, what would you like to know?": "",
  "You said you were researching drones for work. What exactly do you do?": "",
  "Well, I work at an online advertising agency. It's actually a startup company.": "",
  "Wow, that sounds intense. I wonder what that's like.": "",
  "Haha, I get that a lot.": "",
  "I will say we're pretty prolific, mostly because of our work environment. We've even been on TV a few times.": "",
  "It's nice because they let us work at our own pace. Plus our office is really modern... and you should see the cafeteria!": "",
  "As someone who works out of a dingy little hole in the wall... I'm officially jealous.": "",
  "Anyway, what kind of work do you do?": "",
  "Hmm. Mostly writing articles and blogs, as well as event coordinating. I'm basically an advertising director.": "",
  "Haha, you got that right. And frankly, it can be a little draining.": "",
  "Do you have to work a lot of overtime?": "",
  "The question is, do I ever <font_kind=yakuza_italic>not</font_kind> have to work overtime... I can rarely finish all my tasks within a single day.": "",
  "If only I worked more efficiently, I wouldn't have to stay so late all the time.": "",
  "Don't work too hard, now. Otherwise you'll get sick, and then you can't work at all.": "",
  "I appreciate your concern, but I'll be just fine.": "",
  "Yeah... Pretty much...": "",
  "All in all, it sounds like a pretty cool position. I'd say it fits your image.": "",
  "Oh? And what image would that be?": "",
  "Well... stylish, for starters. Someone who cares about both their appearance and their job. Basically the ideal worker.": "",
  "Hah, you flatter me... not that I mind in the least.": "",
  "While we're still on this topic, I'd like to know more about your career. You're the first detective I've met, after all.": "",
  "Well, there are plenty of us detectives out there. Cases, on the other hand, are not as easy to come by.": "",
  "Have you ever dealt with any cases that were... a little out of the norm?": "",
  "Oh, I've had my fair share.": "",
  "Let's see. For example...": "",
  "It was about a year ago. Someone asked me to find a cat. The thing is, it was already supposed to have died.": "",
  "What? You were tasked with finding a dead cat? I don't get it.": "",
  "Apparently, my client saw a cat that looked just like the one they used to own. So they called me in to investigate.": "",
  "Eventually, I found the cat they described. It had this unique sort of fur pattern and it liked to be chased around.": "",
  "So, after chasing it around for what felt like hours, I discovered it was actually the very same cat.": "",
  "What happened was that it wandered into an old lady's house and, thinking it was hers, she kept it and raised it as her own.": "",
  "Wow, so the cat wasn't dead after all? Your client just lost track of it?": "",
  "Yup. Imagine how he felt after finding out his supposedly deceased pet was actually alive and well.": "",
  "Yeah, alive and well in someone else's house. But still, that must've been a relief.": "",
  "More or less. However, there was no way to prove whose cat it actually was.": "",
  "So my client and the old lady were at odds with each other.": "",
  "Then... how did they decide to settle it?": "",
  "With a handshake. You see, the cat knew how to shake hands.": "",
  "No way! Cats can do that?": "",
  "Apparently my client taught it how, so yeah. And when he asked the cat to shake, it did—confirming it was his.": "",
  "Problem was, the old lady had gotten too attached to it. After all, she once had a cat that looked just like it herself.": "",
  "To make matters worse, that cat was the only family she had left. Taking it away from her would've left her devastated.": "",
  "...Poor lady. That's really sad...": "",
  "Yeah, but you know what? The cat seemed to be aware of this, having spent so much time with her.": "",
  "So when it came time for its owner to take it back, the cat wouldn't budge! It just sat there purring on the lady's lap!": "",
  "Really!": "",
  "So it was the one taking care of the old lady, not the other way around... How sweet.": "",
  "My client seemed to think so.": "",
  "And in the end, he parted ways with his pet on her behalf.": "",
  "Yeah, I never saw that coming. But he had a lot of sympathy for her. Maybe it was a cat lover's connection.": "",
  "Sure sounds like it. And their arrangement worked out okay?": "",
  "Oh yeah. It was an outdoors cat to begin with, so my client guessed the cat would come visit him every now and then anyway.": "",
  "Turns out he was right. I hear the cat spends time at both houses now.": "",
  "Wow... Your life is a lot more eventful than I expected. Even when it comes to lost pets!": "",
  "So, what are your hobbies, Nanami-san?": "",
  "Hmm... I really don't have any time for hobbies.": "",
  "The moment I get off work, I go straight home and crash out.": "",
  "Dang. Sounds like you get pretty exhausted.": "",
  "I do. So to answer your question, I guess you could say that work is my hobby.": "",
  "...I must sound like a terribly boring person, don't I...": "",
  "I wouldn't say that. I mean, you can pretty much pick up a hobby any time you want. It's never too late.": "",
  "The idea has crossed my mind, but... nothing ever seems to stick.": "",
  "Well, I guess if you're that busy, you shouldn't really worry about it.": "",
  "Actually, same here. What a funny coincidence.": "",
  "You mean work is your hobby too?": "",
  "Yep. I even work on the weekends, although that's partially because I need to stay open seven days a week to pay rent.": "",
  "...But even though it might seem like my mind's always occupied by work, I'm actually okay with that.": "",
  "That's because detective work is something I enjoy. So I think that qualifies as a hobby.": "",
  "Yeah! I know exactly what you mean!": "",
  "You feel satisfied with life because you're consumed with something that has meaning. Isn't that the best?": "",
  "I think an actual hobby might be good for you. You know, to help take your mind off work every now and then.": "",
  "Well... I understand that, but... I really don't have that kind of time.": "",
  "Not even on the weekends?": "",
  "Nope. I sleep the entire weekend to recover my energy for the next week. That's just how the cycle goes.": "",
  "Guess you're pretty busy then. My mistake.": "",
  "Yagami-san, do you... find your job enjoyable?": "",
  "I'm glad I chose to be a detective.": "",
  "I see. It's important to find satisfaction in your job... as long as you're not overworking yourself 24/7.": "",
  "I can understand that. Sometimes it's healthier to just take it easy.": "",
  "Not sure. It's more of something I do to pay the bills, so... I haven't really given it much thought.": "",
  "I see. I think I understand how you feel.": "",
  "Mind if I ask how old you are?": "",
  "You're asking my age? Just like that?": "",
  "I can't tell you.": "",
  "Aww. Why not?": "",
  "You can't just ask a lady her age and expect to get an answer. It doesn't work like that.": "",
  "Ouch. Am I being scolded right now?": "",
  "You're darn right you are! Hehe, but you know what? I wouldn't mind revealing it to a man I trust.": "",
  "(So she's saying she doesn't trust me... yet.)": "",
  "I'm gonna take a wild guess and say you're in your twenties?": "",
  "...Well, yeah.": "",
  "Your late twenties?": "",
  "You... really want to know my age, don't you?": "",
  "Then, I'm 29.": "",
  "Oh, wow.": "",
  "You look so young for your age.": "",
  "Haha, why thank you. Even if you are just flattering me.": "",
  "Hey now, I was being honest.": "",
  "You're always so well-spoken, and you give off a pretty confident vibe.": "",
  "Well, I am a grown woman.": "",
  "What about you, Yagami-san? I'd say you're in your early thirties?": "",
  "Close enough. I'm 35.": "",
  "Hmm. You look pretty young yourself.": "",
  "Why thank you. Even if you are just flattering me.": "",
  "*giggle* What can I say? I was being honest.": "",
  "I'm glad that stalker of yours is finally out of the picture.": "",
  "Yeah, thanks to you. I almost thought he'd never go away...": "",
  "That just tells you how long he'd been bothering me.": "",
  "Sounds like he was really obsessed.": "",
  "Obsessed is a mild way to put it. He was downright crazy.": "",
  "He would keep asking me out no matter how many times I turned him down... He'd even wait outside my front door...": "",
  "It's like nothing I said ever went through to him!": "",
  "What an awful experience.": "",
  "And when I told the police, you know what they said? \"We can't help you because he hasn't actually done anything.\"": "",
  "Can you believe that? Yagami-san, I was scared for so long...": "",
  "Then I'm glad he's behind bars where he belongs.": "",
  "...So am I. That's why I really mean it when I say you saved my life.": "",
  "I didn't think you'd do so much for me... someone you'd only met once.": "",
  "That actually got me thinking. About what lengths a person should go to help a stranger in need.": "",
  "Ah, I only did what came naturally to me.": "",
  "You mean you acted purely on instinct? ...Are you trying to be some kind of superhero or something?": "",
  "Haha, me, a superhero? I guess I'll take that as a compliment.": "",
  "I wonder though... is that stalker the only guy you've had trouble getting rid of?": "",
  "Well... There have been other instances I'd rather not discuss.": "",
  "But I should tell you this right now: I'm not the type who falls in love easily. To me, work is far more rewarding than romance.": "",
  "Yeah. So playing the whole relationship game doesn't really fit my lifestyle... Just thought I'd get that out there.": "",
  "I'm curious, Nanami-san. What's your philosophy on love?": "",
  "I wouldn't quite call it a philosophy, but...": "",
  "Well, I just think it's all so manufactured. People are always falling in love on TV or in real life, only to break up days later.": "",
  "Everyone talks about romance like it's the number one thing to live for, yet there's so much more to life than just that.": "",
  "Besides, who wants to depend on someone else to make them happy when you can do that on your own? It's unhealthy.": "",
  "I'd have to agree. There's a lot more to life than romance.": "",
  "So you understand me then?": "",
  "Yeah. I think it's important to have some fun and excitement in life, but that doesn't mean it has to come from love.": "",
  "There are plenty of other things that can give you satisfaction, like your hobbies or your career.": "",
  "My thoughts exactly!": "",
  "I get where you're coming from, Nanami-san, but I still think romance has its place.": "",
  "Well, I'm not trying to reject the notion of romance completely...": "",
  "I just don't think it's a necessity. You can live perfectly fine without it.": "",
  "That makes sense. It's not like you need it to breathe or anything.": "",
  "But society seems to think otherwise. No matter who I talk to, I'm always being pressured into finding some guy...": "",
  "And whenever I tell people I'm happy without a man, they look at me like I have a couple screws loose upstairs.": "",
  "I just want to tell them, \"So what! I have plenty of other things to live for!\"": "",
  "Even compared to someone who's in a happy relationship, I still think I have it pretty good. I'm satisfied with me.": "",
  "Well said. As long as you're content with your life, you shouldn't put any extra pressure on yourself.": "",
  "Exactly! Besides, what you decide to do with yourself is the important thing. How you feel comes second.": "",
  "And I second that notion.": "",
  "What's the point of pushing someone into a relationship they don't even need? No one should be that presumptuous.": "",
  "Ahh, I'm so glad you understand! I feel like you're the only one who gets me.": "",
  "If that's really how you think, then I'm in deep trouble.": "",
  "Trouble? How so?": "",
  "Well... that means I can't date you.": "",
  "I'm... I'm sorry?": "",
  "...Oh, I get it. You're teasing me, aren't you?": "",
  "Haha, just a bit. But seriously, Nanami-san. I know what you mean.": "",
  "Yeah. I feel the same way.": "",
  "The idea that there's this void in your life unless you \"find your other half\" is really contrived and overdone.": "",
  "I'm honestly quite shocked. I never thought I'd actually meet someone—let alone a guy—who thinks the same as me!": "",
  "Yeah! Yagami-san, you and I are definitely on the same wavelength!": "",
  "(Well, that's great... But given that we're kind of out on a date, that might not be the greatest wavelength to be on.)": "",
  "Oh yeah. While we're at it, why don't we take a picture together?": "",
  "For old time's sake? Haha, sure, why not.": "",
  "Okay... Let's see how it turned out.": "",
  "(Mm, looks good. I'll send this to her later.)": "",
  "Hmm, I think we can do better than this. Mind if we try again?": "",
  "Well. Shall we get going?": "",
  "Yeah, I think so. Look at the time already!": "",
  "Thank you for taking me out today, Yagami-san.": "",
  "It was my pleasure. Thanks for coming with.": "",
  "Did you have fun with me today?": "",
  "The most I've had in a long time, Nanami-san.": "",
  "Haha, then I'm glad we went out.": "",
  "Huh? Nanami, is that you...?": "",
  "Hmm?": "",
  "I knew it! Nanami, I haven't seen you in forever!": "",
  "Wait... Yukko? Is that you?": "",
  "Who else!? Gosh, it's been what... since we graduated college? Feels like that was <font_kind=yakuza_italic>ages</font_kind> ago!": "",
  "I know, right? What brings you to Kamurocho, anyway?": "",
  "Oh, I actually work nearby!": "",
  "Who's your friend, Nanami-san?": "",
  "Oh, this is Yukko. We've known each other since middle school.": "",
  "Hey, Yukko? Do you remember that time when we...": "",
  "Uh. Yukko?": "",
  "So... handsome...": "",
  "Forget handsome—this guy's <font_kind=yakuza_italic>hot</font_kind>! Like, 110 degrees!": "",
  "In fact, just looking at him is burning me up inside... Ahh, what should I do!? ❤": "",
  "H-Hey, Yukko! Get a hold of yourself!": "",
  "Wait, don't tell me... is this fine specimen of a man right here your boyfriend!?": "",
  "...Boyfriend? I have no idea what you're talking about.": "",
  "Nanami... I'm so proud of you. You finally decided to move on...": "",
  "Move on from what? Is there something I should know about?": "",
  "Don't listen to her, Yagami-san! She's just a little... confused.": "",
  "Now listen here, Yukko. He and I are nothing more than—": "",
  "Oh, no, I understand! I wouldn't want to get in the way of your <font_kind=yakuza_italic>private time</font_kind>!": "",
  "Well then, Mr. Handsome. You be sure to treat Nanami right, okay? 'Cause if you don't, you'll be facing some serious trouble!": "",
  "Got it... I think.": "",
  "Good. Now I'll see you two lovebirds later!": "",
  "Huh. Interesting friend you got there.": "",
  "Sorry. She's always been a little on the <font_kind=yakuza_italic>eccentric</font_kind> side.": "",
  "It's been a while since I last saw her... and she hasn't changed one bit.": "",
  "Thank you for today, Yagami-san. I hope you had a good time.": "",
  "As for me, I actually really enjoyed myself.": "",
  "Yeah! I hope you'll share more stories with me in the future.": "",
  "I'd be happy to.": "",
  "Thank you for today, Yagami-san. I hope you had fun...": "",
  "Did you have fun, Nanami-san?": "",
  "Oh! Well...": "",
  "Uh, of course I did!": "",
  "I've never talked to a detective before. So I guess we had a... stimulating conversation?": "",
  "(She doesn't sound very enthusiastic... Maybe it wasn't that much fun for her?)": "",
  "*giggle* Hello there, Mr. Handsome. I'm back! ❤": "",
  "Hey there, ladies.": "",
  "Let me give you a proper introduction this time. This is Yukiko Tonegawa, but you can call her Yukko for short.": "",
  "Nice to officially meet you! Let's see... so I work at an office in Tokyo...": "",
  "I'm 29 years old... and currently on the hunt for a nice, good-looking boyfriend!": "",
  "And this here's Yagami-san. He's a detective in Kamurocho.": "",
  "Nice to meet you. First name's Takayuki, and I'm 35.": "",
  "...W-What is it?": "",
  "Oh, nothing! I was just thinking you're a real feast for the eyes!": "",
  "Uh... thank you?": "",
  "In case you didn't catch it earlier, Yukko's currently single.": "",
  "She's also pretty cute, isn't she?": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "Yeah. I feel the same way.": "เออ ฉันก็รู้สึกเหมือนกันนะ",
  "Hmm?": "หือ?"
 }
}
